  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">RURAL ACTION FOR CLIMATE RESILIENCE PROJECT</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Rural Action for Climate Resilience (RACR) project in South Africa, implemented by the Social Change Assistance Trust (SCAT) in partnership with SAFCEI, aims to strengthen climate resilience in rural communities. The objectives of the grant are to empower community- and faith-based organisations, particularly women- and youth-led groups, to adopt locally led climate adaptation solutions and influence climate policy processes. The key activities include micro-grants for climate resilience initiatives, technical mentorship, peer learning, youth engagement, and climate advocacy, delivered in collaboration with rural partners across five provinces.</narrative>
  </description>
